# SolidJS + TypeScript in this client

This is **SolidJS 1.9.14** (pinned in `pnpm-workspace.yaml` — do not bump it; newer 1.9.x broke
reactivity across packages). It is not React. Components run once; reactivity lives in signals.

## Reactivity

- Never destructure props. Read `props.x` where you need it, or use `splitProps` / `mergeProps`.
  Destructuring breaks reactivity silently. (`eslint-plugin-solid` will flag most cases.)
- Derived values are functions: `const label = () => props.name ?? t\`Unknown\``. Call them in JSX.
- Use `createSignal`, `createMemo`, `createEffect`, `createResource`, `onCleanup`. No React hooks,
  no `useState`, no `useEffect`, no dependency arrays.
- Control flow: `<Show>`, `<For>`, `<Index>`, `<Switch>/<Match>`, `<Dynamic>`. Do not use
  `array.map` in JSX for lists that change, and do not use `&&` / ternaries for conditional blocks
  that own state.
- Clean up listeners, timers and observers with `onCleanup`.
- Data from `stoat.js` objects is already reactive; read fields inside JSX or memos, not once at
  component start.

## Styling

- Panda CSS: `css({...})`, `styled(...)`, `cva(...)` from `styled-system/*`. Use theme tokens
  (`var(--md-sys-color-*)`, spacing tokens) instead of raw hex or px where a token exists.
- `styled-system/` is generated by `panda codegen`. Never edit it.
- Layout must work at 390px wide with no horizontal scroll, and in light and dark themes.

## Imports and modules

- Import shared code through workspace aliases: `@revolt/ui`, `@revolt/client`, `@revolt/i18n`,
  `@revolt/routing`, `@revolt/state`, `@revolt/modal`, etc. Avoid deep relative paths across packages.
- Use `import type` for type-only imports (required for `stoat.js` types inside `@revolt/ui`).
- Icons: `@material-design-icons/svg/...` or `@material-symbols/svg-400/...` with
  `?component-solid` is fine. **Do not** import an SVG that contains `<text>` with
  `?component-solid` — `vite-plugin-solid-svg` drops text nodes. Write it as a JSX component
  instead (see `components/ui/components/design/AmixofWordmark.tsx`).
- Do not add a dependency for something a few lines of code can do. If you must add one, use
  `pnpm --filter client add <pkg>` and commit the lockfile.

## TypeScript

- No `any` unless you write why. Prefer narrowing, `satisfies`, and exact types.
- No `// @ts-ignore`. If unavoidable, use `// @ts-expect-error <reason>`.
- `pnpm --filter client exec tsc --noEmit` must pass.

## Code style (from GUIDELINES.md)

- Prettier formats everything (2 spaces, organize-imports). Run it; don't hand-format.
- Put a short doc comment above every component, exported function, class, and constant.
- Semantic HTML, real `<button>`s, labels on inputs, `aria-label` on icon-only buttons,
  keyboard reachable, visible focus.
- Re-export third-party libraries from one place instead of importing them in many components.

## Common traps

- Placeholder env values (`__VITE_API_URL__` etc.) are replaced at container start. Do not
  hard-code production URLs in source; read `import.meta.env` through `components/common/lib/env.ts`.
- Anything gated by `instance.isStoat` / `STOAT_HOST` never shows on amixof.com. Do not
  "fix" branding inside those branches unless you also change the gate.
- The service worker caches old bundles. When checking a deploy in a browser, use a fresh
  profile or hard refresh.
